# Whole-word and regular-expression saved-file search

This is a separate work-only development epoch. Existing literal defaults, saved UTF-8 filesystem limits, exact byte revisions, path contract, dirty-draft preservation, search/read generations and corrected Save publication stay bound to the copied current sources. Earlier140/124/126 and Save epochs remain historical and unchanged. No current application, public result, registry or root runner changes here.

The proposed API adds boolean `wholeWord` and `useRegex` options, default false, and accessible in-page toggles. Pinned VS Code1.140.0 source derives whole-word patterns through `createRegExp`, then the workspace engine applies `--crlf`, source Unicode/newline conversions and engine auto selection. This is not equivalent to blindly passing `--word-regexp`; pattern edge/alternation cases are explicit helper targets. The new runtime uses newly written standard-library code, never an original executable/module. Selected complete MIT source files and exact acquisition/engine identities remain verification-only.

Regex execution/compilation will be isolated in a request-scoped worker with bounded query/content/output/active-worker budgets, an observed timeout/termination/exit lifecycle and no main-thread untrusted expression. The supported language is JavaScript Unicode single-line regex plus explicitly documented common Unicode-class/boundary normalization. Full Rust/PCRE2 syntax, multiline matching, original service/workbench behavior, include/exclude/ignore settings, remote workspaces and unsaved-buffer search remain open. Resource caps are not a whole-machine memory watchdog; parent scheduling and OS calls can delay wall-clock completion. Invalid patterns and worker/budget failures must be explicit and retain bounded partial results or errors, never silent complete empty success.

Predeclared finite evidence targets: whole-word ASCII/punctuation/Unicode/combining/join-control edges; regex anchors/alternation/classes/quantifiers/case/Unicode; zero-length matches including empty and CRLF lines, surrogate pairs and adjacency; invalid patterns and bounded output; exact UTF-16 line/column/start/end navigation; options or a later query invalidating held results/reads; dirty/stale snapshots and held Save responses preserving newer drafts; worker timeout/error/close/disposal and aggregate active-worker refusal. Direct original bundled-ripgrep calls will be bounded, authenticated and counted separately from selected original source-helper evaluation and from original GUI0. Every initial mismatch/failure remains retained; no benchmark or performance acceptance.

Root approved this candidate-only scope and separately announced its full847 suite closed before allowing selected comparisons/stress. Preparation source acquisition and copying execute no application/original behavior. A delegation follow-up was attempted but rejected by the agent-thread limit; no new delegated source review ran.
